      "reason": "WRONG RIG — measured, not assumed. The pack downloads fine (lib/itch-fetch.sh, free upload, LICENSE.txt inside reads 'License: (Creative Commons Zero, CC0)'), but Animations/gltf/KayKit_AnimatedCharacter_v1.2.glb is the blocky 'PrototypePete' demo character on a 6-JOINT rig, while the KayKit Adventurers/Skeletons characters we ship are a 41-bone rig. Its 30 clips therefore cannot drive the shipped characters without a rig-aware retarget (Blender / a BoneMap authored in the Godot editor). The 76-clip library already extracted from the Adventurers pack is on the CORRECT rig and covers the social poses this room needs (Idle, Cheer, Sit_Chair_*, Sit_Floor_*, Lie_*, Interact, PickUp, Throw, Walking/Running variants). Only Wave/Dance/Climbing/Hop/Roll are unique to the standalone pack — recorded as a follow-up for a Blender-equipped machine rather than shipped as clips nothing can play."
